  "briefing": "[b]Act 1: the Solar Age.[/b] Your people have just learned to live and work beyond their homeworld. The whole map is your home system: the sun at its heart, rocky inner worlds, your homeworld, marginal worlds a Colony Ship can settle, an asteroid belt, gas giants with icy moons and the cold outer dark.\n\n[b]Every body is claimed on its own.[/b] Fly a ship to a body (or next to it) to [b]survey[/b] it and see its traits. A [b]Colony Ship[/b] settles a habitable world; a [b]Constructor[/b] builds mining bases on rocks and belts, research stations on ice and gas, or a plain outpost. Click a body you hold, or select a ship parked on one and press [b]S[/b], to open it.\n\n[b]Not everyone wants your government.[/b] Separatists hold a fortified base out among the moons, and alien scavengers have made a lair in the outer system. Both send raiders to plunder your outposts while their bases stand; storming a base pays loot.\n\n[b]Goal:[/b] research [b]Hyperdrive[/b] (the last era of the tech tree) to wake the dormant jump points at the edge of the system and end Act 1. Lose everything and the campaign is over.\n\n[b]Controls[/b]: click a fleet, then a blue hex. [b]S[/b] open a body, [b]T[/b] tech tree, [b]E[/b] Empire, [b]H[/b] Heroes, [b]Space[/b] end turn, [b]Esc[/b] menu.",
